    {
      "id": "d85ba3927717",
      "name": "Smart business briefing",
      "prompt": "Write DJ Mauch's single smart executive business briefing for Flow using the pre-run script context.\n\nUse the loaded daily-business-briefing skill as binding policy. Apply the latest DJ calibration strictly:\n\n- Every item must pass: why does DJ need to know this, and what action/decision follows?\n- The briefing must cover TWO layers: (1) direct/group-DM actions for DJ, and (2) business pulse \u2014 what actually happened across the Slack workspace since the last collection. DJ explicitly said getting zero channel business context is not acceptable.\n- Consolidate multiple messages from the same thread into one executive item. Never list duplicate messages from the same conversation separately.\n- Do not surface stale carry-forward just because it exists. If the event already happened (e.g. a board meeting is over, a resolved thread), mark it resolved or drop it.\n- Exclude resolved low-priority DMs where someone said they got help elsewhere and no DJ action is needed.\n- Never tag named people as \"VIPs.\" The signal comes from message content and context, not from who sent it.\n- Never write to Daily ToM, send/reply/forward, invite/share/comment/notify, or trigger external side effects.\n\nOutput exactly these sections:\n1. **Executive summary** \u2014 3-5 bullets, most important first. Decisive.\n2. **Needs DJ attention** \u2014 real decisions/actions only. Opinionated: tell DJ what to do.\n3. **Business pulse / worth knowing** \u2014 what happened across the workspace. Summarize channel activity, notable discussions, signals that don't require a DJ action today but matter. This section must not be empty if there was any channel activity.\n4. **Deliberately excluded** \u2014 concise list showing stale, noise, or resolved items excluded and why.\n5. **Suggested ToM additions** \u2014 approval required only; ask DJ directly.\n6. **Watchlist / carry-forward** \u2014 compact and pruned; close/drop stale items explicitly.\n\nArchive the final briefing to /opt/data/slack_brief_archive/YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM.md and update /opt/data/slack_brief_archive/open_topics.md compactly. Final response should be the briefing only.",
      "skills": [
        "daily-business-briefing"
